# PART 2 — ROLE-SPECIFIC PORTAL LOCKDOWN

The lockdown should resemble the Microsoft Office activation experience: the account can still open the permitted parts of the portal, but restricted features are visibly disabled.

Do not make the interface look broken or display endless loading indicators.

Show a deliberate, professional lockdown screen or banner explaining the exact reason and the action required.

## 2.1 School administrator lockdown

A school administrator whose institutional subscription has exceeded the grace period must retain access to:

- Basic school dashboard/overview.
- Billing Center.
- Payment history and available invoices/receipts.
- Subscription details.
- Pay Now action.
- Account and contact details needed to resolve billing.

The following school features must be locked:

- Student roster.
- Student profiles and personal information.
- Class schedules.
- Resources panel and resource downloads.
- Examination management and results.
- Assessment management.
- Passcodes.
- Student reports.
- Results printing and exporting.
- Other restricted school operational dashboards.

The restrictions must apply to both navigation and direct URLs.

### Visual behaviour

When the administrator enters the school portal:

- Display a prominent but professional lockdown notice.
- Clearly show: **PORTAL CURRENTLY ON LOCKDOWN — PAYMENT OVERDUE.**
- Display the outstanding payment amount and due date where available.
- Provide a prominent **PAY NOW** action.
- Keep Billing accessible.
- Keep the permitted basic dashboard accessible.
- Grey out restricted navigation items and make them non-interactive.
- Display a lock indicator beside restricted sections.

When the administrator clicks a restricted feature, show a clear explanation:

"Your school portal is currently on lockdown because the institutional subscription has not been renewed. Please complete your outstanding payment to restore access."

The Pay Now action must open the school's existing Billing Center, not an unrelated payment page.

Do not expose student names, roster information, examination information, or schedules on the locked overview page.

## 2.2 School student lockdown

A school student's subscription entitlement must inherit the payment status of the school-funded programme or institution.

When the school administrator's institutional subscription becomes locked after the seven-day grace period:

- School students may still authenticate and log in.
- Their academic data must not load.
- Their assignments, resources, assessments, results, schedules and learning materials must not load.
- They must not be able to print or download restricted academic records.
- The portal should display a dedicated lockdown screen.

Display:

**YOUR SCHOOL PORTAL IS CURRENTLY ON LOCKDOWN**

"Your school's institutional subscription has not been renewed. Please contact your school administrator for further information."

Do not show students a payment button for an institutional payment that belongs to their school.

Do not allow school students to make payments on behalf of the school.

Once the school subscription is successfully renewed and verified, the students' access should automatically return without requiring an administrator to manually unlock every student account.

## 2.3 Individually enrolled student lockdown

An independently enrolled student is responsible for their own programme subscription.

During the seven-day grace period, allow access and show appropriate renewal notices.

After seven full days overdue:

Keep accessible:
- Basic student dashboard.
- Billing Center.
- Outstanding balance.
- Payment history.
- Pay Now.
- Relevant account information.

Lock:
- Learning materials and programme content.
- Assignments and activities.
- Assessments and examinations.
- Results and reports.
- Restricted class resources.
- Other features that require an active programme subscription.

Display:

**YOUR LEARNING PORTAL IS CURRENTLY ON LOCKDOWN**

"Your current programme subscription has expired and has not been renewed. Please complete your payment to continue learning."

Provide a **PAY NOW** action that opens the student's own Billing Center.

Do not redirect payment responsibility to a school or parent unless the student's actual billing responsibility says that the parent pays.

## 2.4 Parent and parent-enrolled student lockdown

The parent is responsible for payment for parent-funded children.

When the parent's relevant payment obligation exceeds the seven-day grace period:

### Parent account

The parent must still be able to:
- Sign in.
- Open the basic account overview.
- Open Billing.
- Review outstanding fee items.
- See the affected child's name and programme.
- View payment history.
- Make payments.
- View relevant invoices and receipts.

The parent must not be able to access restricted child learning content while the corresponding fee obligation is locked.

Restrict the affected child's:
- Resources.
- Assignments.
- Activities.
- Assessments.
- Examination results.
- Learning tracks and paid programme features.
- Reports and restricted downloads.

Display:

**YOUR CHILD'S LEARNING ACCESS IS CURRENTLY ON LOCKDOWN**

"Payment for your child's current programme is overdue. Please complete the outstanding payment to restore learning access."

Provide **PAY NOW** and direct the parent to the correct fee item in the Billing Center.

### Parent-enrolled student account

The child must still be able to sign in, but academic data must not load while their parent-funded entitlement is locked.

Display:

**YOUR LEARNING PORTAL IS CURRENTLY ON LOCKDOWN**

"Your learning access is temporarily unavailable because the payment for your programme has not been renewed. Please contact your parent or guardian for more information."

Do not show a Pay Now action on the child account. The parent is the payer.

### Multiple children

Preserve the existing parent-child relationship model.

Where fee obligations are tracked separately for different children or programmes, lock the affected child/programme rather than unnecessarily blocking access to another child's fully paid programme.

Where the existing parent contract is explicitly a single account-level subscription covering all children, apply lockdown consistently to that contract.

Never expose or modify records belonging to another parent.

## 2.5 Funding-responsibility precedence

Enforce the following rules:

| Learner type | Who pays? | What triggers lockdown? |
|---|---|---|
| School administrator | School | School subscription overdue beyond grace period |
| School-funded student | School | Parent institution's school subscription becomes locked |
| Individually enrolled student | Student | Their personal subscription becomes locked |
| Parent-enrolled student | Parent/guardian | The relevant parent-funded fee obligation becomes locked |
| School student with a self-funded additional programme | Student for the additional programme | That additional programme's own unpaid obligation |

A school must not receive a bill for a student's independently purchased programme.

A parent must not be charged for a school-funded programme merely because the parent has an account connected to the student.

Preserve all existing student registration categories and their account relationships.

