## 6.3 Atomic updates and audit trail

When an administrator records a manual payment, perform the payment record and corresponding subscription/balance updates atomically where possible.

The action should:
1. Create the manual payment record.
2. Update the correct fee item.
3. Update the subscription period if the obligation has been satisfied.
4. Recalculate the remaining balance.
5. Re-evaluate lockdown.
6. Restore access if the payment qualifies.
7. Record an administrative audit entry.

Prevent accidental duplicate manual payment entries.

Show who recorded the payment and when.

If a payment is reversed or corrected, preserve the audit trail. Do not silently edit historical successful payment records.

