# PART 8 — TUTOR-MANAGED CLASS MEETING LINKS

Add a flexible class meeting-link management feature to the existing tutor scheduling workflow.

The requirement is that tutors can configure the meeting link for each scheduled class, including different links for different weeks.

For example:

| Week | Class date | Meeting link |
|---|---|---|
| Week 1 | 1 December | Microsoft Teams link A |
| Week 2 | 8 December | Microsoft Teams link B |
| Week 3 | 15 December | Microsoft Teams link C |
| Week 4 | 22 December | Microsoft Teams link C |

A tutor may also choose to retain the same meeting link for every week.

## 8.1 Per-session link configuration

Inspect the existing `classSchedules` structure and the current schedule creation and editing interfaces.

The existing schedule model already supports a `meetingLink` field in `SchoolClassScheduleTimeline.tsx`.

Extend the existing system so that an authorized tutor can:

- Add a meeting link to an individual class.
- Edit the link for a future class.
- Change the link for a particular week without changing other weeks.
- Leave the same link in place for future weeks.
- Apply one link to multiple selected future classes.
- Choose whether an edit applies to only one occurrence or to selected future occurrences.

Do not automatically overwrite historical class meeting links when a tutor changes a future session.

## 8.2 Link inheritance

Where recurring class schedules or schedule groups exist, support a sensible inheritance model:

- A recurring group may have a default meeting link.
- An individual occurrence may override that link.
- If the tutor does not provide a new link for an occurrence, it can inherit the existing default.
- A tutor can replace the default for future classes without changing historical occurrences.
- The interface must make it clear whether the link is inherited or individually configured.

Do not create unnecessary duplicate schedule records simply to store different meeting links.

## 8.3 Permissions and validation

Only:
- The tutor assigned to that class or programme.
- Authorized platform administrators.

may change its meeting link.

School administrators and students should not be able to alter tutor-controlled meeting links unless an existing explicit administrative permission allows it.

Validate links using the existing meeting-link validation logic in `src/lib/scheduleEngine.ts`.

Support Microsoft Teams, Google Meet, Zoom and other valid HTTPS meeting platforms.

Record:
- Who created or changed the link.
- When it was changed.
- The affected schedule occurrence.
- Whether it is an inherited or individual link.

The student, parent and school schedule interfaces should always display the correct current link for the relevant class date.

Ensure the link displayed to a learner is the link for that exact scheduled occurrence, not merely the most recent link saved for the entire programme.

